From: YANG JOO WOONG <yjw.cpa@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Jun 2026 22:00:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] PCI/P2PDMA: Add Intel Broadwell-EP to the whitelist

Intel Broadwell-EP (Xeon E5 v4, device 0x6f00/0x6f01) supports P2P
routing through the root complex, same as its predecessor Haswell-EP
(0x2f00) and successor Skylake-E (0x2030). The omission from the
whitelist is an oversight — NVIDIA SLI on X99 + PLX PEX8747 confirmed
P2P DMA works on this platform.

Add with REQ_SAME_HOST_BRIDGE flag consistent with Haswell-EP entry.

Signed-off-by: YANG JOO WOONG <yjw.cpa@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pci/p2pdma.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/p2pdma.c b/drivers/pci/p2pdma.c
index 1a20948..b2c3f4d 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/p2pdma.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/p2pdma.c
@@ -36,6 +36,9 @@ static const struct {
 	/* Intel Xeon E7 v3/Xeon E5 v3/Core i7 */
 	{PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL,	0x2f00, REQ_SAME_HOST_BRIDGE},
 	{PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL,	0x2f01, REQ_SAME_HOST_BRIDGE},
+	/* Intel Xeon E5 v4 (Broadwell-EP) */
+	{PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL,	0x6f00, REQ_SAME_HOST_BRIDGE},
+	{PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL,	0x6f01, REQ_SAME_HOST_BRIDGE},
 	/* Intel Skylake-E */
 	{PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL,	0x2030, 0},
 	{PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL,	0x2031, 0},
--
2.49.0
